Open Command Prompt.

Create a new directory:

mkdir pgm3

Move to the directory:

cd pgm3

Initialize Gradle project:

gradle init

Select the following options:
Build Type: Application
Implementation Language: Groovy
Java Version: 21 (or available version)
Project Structure: Single Application Project
Build Script DSL: Kotlin
Wait until BUILD SUCCESSFUL message appears.

Run the project using:

gradlew run

To view project structure, use:

tree

COMMANDS:

mkdir pgm3
cd pgm3
gradle init
gradlew run
tree

OUTPUT:

Hello World!

RESULT:
Successfully created and executed a Gradle project using Groovy/Kotlin DSL and Gradle build scripts.
